              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The respondent is accused of a homicide in which he entered the victim\u2019s room armed, delivered fatal blows, and later attempted to conceal the crime."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "70d39f661b3443e17daab11b2e8dfa74e4d148a891aa40d7df2a6159a34f5393",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-70d39f661b34-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked: \u201cWhen there is an evidentiary hearing, how does the standard for the court of appeals differ than when there has been no evidentiary hearing?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "70d39f661b3443e17daab11b2e8dfa74e4d148a891aa40d7df2a6159a34f5393",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-70d39f661b34-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 15,
              "start": 15
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts raised the issue of the \u201cnothing to lose\u201d rule, asking why the Court had not addressed it directly."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "70d39f661b3443e17daab11b2e8dfa74e4d148a891aa40d7df2a6159a34f5393",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-70d39f661b34-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia questioned whether the issue was an \u201cunreasonable application of clearly established Supreme Court law.\u201d"
      }
    ],
