  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "70d39f661b3443e17daab11b2e8dfa74e4d148a891aa40d7df2a6159a34f5393",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-70d39f661b34-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the dispute centers on whether, under the Antiterrorism and Effective Death Penalty Act (ADPA), the respondent is entitled to federal habeas corpus relief on an ineffective\u2011counsel claim."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "70d39f661b3443e17daab11b2e8dfa74e4d148a891aa40d7df2a6159a34f5393",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-70d39f661b34-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner argues that the ADPA requires state courts to be the primary forum for such claims, funneling them through the state system first."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Sevilla",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "70d39f661b3443e17daab11b2e8dfa74e4d148a891aa40d7df2a6159a34f5393",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-70d39f661b34-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Sevilla, the transcript also contains discussion of the \u201cnothing to lose\u201d rule, which some counsel describe as a fictional doctrine."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "70d39f661b3443e17daab11b2e8dfa74e4d148a891aa40d7df2a6159a34f5393",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-70d39f661b34-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 11,
              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to the court record, the respondent allegedly entered the victim\u2019s room with a gun, inflicted fatal blows, and later disposed of evidence and fabricated an alibi."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "70d39f661b3443e17daab11b2e8dfa74e4d148a891aa40d7df2a6159a34f5393",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-70d39f661b34-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, under the deferential review required by the ADPA, the respondent is not entitled to federal habeas relief on his ineffective\u2011counsel claim because the state court\u2019s adjudication was not contrary to, nor an unreasonable application of, the Strickland test."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "70d39f661b3443e17daab11b2e8dfa74e4d148a891aa40d7df2a6159a34f5393",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-70d39f661b34-0000-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 10,
                "start": 10
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the ADPA intends that all such claims be funneled through state courts, which are the primary interpreters and enforcers of federal constitutional law for state prisoners."
        }
      ],
